-- Inbox review 2026-11-04 (PRs #339-#368): the research server kept re-checking the same towns. What came out of it:
-- Mahjong Republic (Carlsbad): its class page says "how to read the NMJL card" and its event list calls the beginner class "an intro to American Mahjong"; studio inside Pickleball Republic. Carlsbad was already published.
-- Coastal Virginia Mahjong (Virginia Beach): the booking page titles its sessions "Open Play - American Mahjong" (own wording; the NMJL is not named), at Seacoast Academy; seven active rows, so Virginia Beach is published.
-- Mahj Brooklyn (instructor, listed under New York): its own site says "Mahj Brooklyn offers American mahjong instruction across Brooklyn and Manhattan".
-- Not taken: Friendswood (Hall's Hall is still not confirmed as a public venue), Fair Game Downers Grove (no American wording), Bridgeport library (no American / NMJL wording), the Honolulu leads (private condo, no current course), and the Brooklyn / Ypsilanti library and teacher leads (no own-page wording).
UPDATE "Club" SET "status" = 'ACTIVE', "lastVerifiedAt" = '2026-11-04', "website" = 'https://coastalvirginiamahjong.bamgoodtime.com', "address" = 'Seacoast Academy, 968 First Colonial Rd, Ste 104, Virginia Beach, VA 23454', "description" = 'Its own booking page lists its sessions as "Open Play - American Mahjong" and a "Mahjong Beginner Class" at Seacoast Academy on First Colonial Road, plus seasonal socials at local restaurants. Registration is handled externally from the booking page.' WHERE "slug" = 'virginia-beach-coastal-virginia-mahjong';
